  "dom_id": "step-q121903",
  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "The velocity vector $v=\u27e8u,v\u27e9$ of a particle $P$ at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\nv=\u27e8\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(3t+2),\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(2t+5)\u27e9,\\,t>0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the acceleration vector $a.$",
  "worked_solution": "To compute the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\u27e8\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(3t+2)),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(2t+5))\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8\\frac{3}{3t+2},2\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(2t+5)\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$",
